        {
          "id": 1704390657,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Heavy (personal) user case is for SIP messaging.  Copy as C string yields the following:\n\n```\n\"SIP/2.0 200 OK\\x0d\\x0aVia: SIP/2.0/UDP 10.174.5.234:5090;branch=z9hG4bK1333.e99c90c7000000000000000000000000.0\\x0d\\x0aTo: <sip:usrloc@10.174.5.232:5090>;tag=356054a66ca753f78ca0b39bb3b9638e.00fa7c11\\x0d\\x0aFrom: <sip:usrloc@10.174.5.234:5090>;tag=9fc2547d6604be6c0c691a214eaaa3e7-e6217fb8\\x0d\\x0aCSeq: 10 KDMQ\\x0d\\x0aCall-ID: 09ed7b1b75f960db-21@10.174.5.234\\x0d\\x0aContent-Length: 0\\x0d\\x0a\\x0d\\x0a\"\n```\n\nWhile it's not difficult to change instances of `\\x0d\\x0a` to new line characters,  I'm frequently copying and pasting messages into chats, emails, etc to communicate message details to other people, so this is a time killer.\n\nPlease undo the feature removal? :)",
          "author": {
            "id": 14287275,
            "username": "bkaufman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Ben Kaufman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/14287275/avatar.png?v=1789095699",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/bkaufman"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-21T15:08:29.663Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-21T15:08:29.663Z",
          "system": false,
