    {
      "id": "16db6e90265ae96ec4eb1d1d1df3e300f964660c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1663070155,
          "type": null,
          "body": "From strings(1) manual:\n```\nFor each file given, GNU strings prints the printable character\nsequences that are at least 4 characters long (or the number given with\nthe options below) and are followed by an unprintable character.\n```\nLater:\n```\n       --encoding=encoding\n           Select  the character encoding of the strings that are to be found.\n           Possible values for encoding are: s = single-7-bit-byte  characters\n           (default),  S = single-8-bit-byte characters, b = 16-bit bigendian,\n           l  =  16-bit  littleendian,  B  =  32-bit  bigendian,  L  =  32-bit\n           littleendian.   Useful for finding wide character strings. (l and b\n           apply to, for example, Unicode UTF-16/UCS-2 encodings).\n```\n\nI distinctly remember getting mojibake when I used the now removed \"printable text\" action on an UTF-8 string field value.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-22T23:19:35.637Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-22T23:19:35.637Z",
